meta {
  name: End subject assignment
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/teacher-assignments/{{subjectTeacherAssignmentId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "valid_to": "2026-10-31",
    "status": "completed"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq completed
  res.body.subject_offering_id: eq {{electiveOfferingId}}
}

docs {
  A teacher who hands over mid-year is dated out, not deleted. Who taught whom
  and when is what makes a mark defensible a year later, so the row survives
  with an end date on it.

  valid_to cannot fall before valid_from; the pair is checked on every write.
  Note what ending an assignment does to access: it is the assignment that
  grants a teacher sight of pupils, so closing this one narrows what that
  teacher may read from here on, without touching anything they wrote before.

  There is no GET /teacher-assignments/{id}. An assignment is read as a
  teacher's timetable, which 06/03 lists.
}
